<title>UK: Courts says trading &quot;quite encouraging&quot;.</title>
<headline>Courts says trading &quot;quite encouraging&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK household furnishing retailer Courts Plc said on Wednesday it was benefitting from a consumer &quot;feel-good&quot; factor, adding that trading in Britain had been &quot;quite encouraging&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;Overseas, with very few exceptions, we have also shown satisfactory progress in most countries where we operate,&quot; Chairman Paul Cohen told shareholders at the annual meeting.  </p>
<p>The company was continuing to expand some of its superstores with one in Liverpool having opened recently and stores in Altrincham, Doncaster, Bradford, Coventry and Birmingham due to open this financial year, he said.</p>
<p>Cohen noted that a new superstore in Dublin had opened &quot;most successfully&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
